Package: urpssim
Title: Urogynecology Workforce Supply and Demand Microsimulation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A stochastic, individual-level microsimulation of the supply of and
    demand for urogynecology and reconstructive pelvic surgery (URPS) services in
    the United States. Supply is projected from an individual provider roster
    using age- and sex-specific hours worked, retirement and career-change
    hazards, and geographic placement. Demand is projected from age-banded
    population series through service volumes and a work-RVU workload conversion
    to required full-time-equivalent providers, so supply and demand are always
    compared in the same units. The base-year supply shortfall is estimated
    rather than assumed. Methods follow the IHS Markit / Dall Health Workforce
    Microsimulation Model and its published applications in physiatry, neurology
    and physical therapy.
